Close what a stopped run left open from the leaves up, and survive one close
failing. Teardown drained subagents before tools, so a tool belonging to a
subagent ended after the subagent span it sits inside — a bar sticking out past
its parent, which happens whenever a run is interrupted while a delegation has a
tool running. None of the close loops guarded an individual span either: one
invocation raising as it finished left the agent span recording and never
exported, and the exception escaped into the caller's `async for`, where it looks
like the transport failing and can mask a real transport error.
